From: mpenelange <191051681+mpenelange@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: jail: hold signals until the handlers are installed

procd signals an instance right after (re)starting it on a reload (dnsmasq's
reload_service: start_service, then procd_send_signal). ujail installs its
handlers only in signals_init(), after option and OCI parsing, so a SIGHUP in
that window killed it with the default action; procd counted a crash and,
after five within the hour, stopped respawning: dnsmasq stayed down, and with
it DNS and DHCP for every network. Seen on the ER-4 (1 GHz MIPS) whenever
a new network was applied.

Most of the window is before main() even runs (the dynamic loader on a slow
CPU), so procd starts a jailed instance with all signals blocked (the mask
survives execve), ujail also blocks them first thing in main() for other
callers, and signals_init() unblocks them once the handlers are in place,
before any process is spawned (the jailed process inherits the mask). A
signal that arrives before the jailed process runs is dropped, as it already
was between signals_init() and the spawn.

--- a/jail/jail.c	2026-10-17 17:58:08.271284563 -0500
+++ b/jail/jail.c	2026-10-17 17:58:08.283284558 -0500
@@ -1159,6 +1159,10 @@
 		s.sa_handler = jail_handle_signal;
 		sigaction(i, &s, NULL);
 	}
+	/* handlers are in place: deliver what main() held back (forwarded, or dropped while
+	 * nothing runs yet), and don't hand a blocked mask to the jailed process */
+	sigemptyset(&sigmask);
+	sigprocmask(SIG_SETMASK, &sigmask, NULL);
 }
 
 static void pre_exec_jail(struct uloop_timeout *t);
@@ -2601,6 +2605,13 @@
 	struct list_head envl = LIST_HEAD_INIT(envl);
 	struct env_e *enve, *tmpenve;
 	unsigned short int envn = 0, envc = 0;
+	sigset_t allsig;
+
+	/* until signals_init(), a signal would take its default action: a reload's SIGHUP from
+	 * procd right after it (re)started the instance killed ujail, procd counted a crash, and
+	 * after five it stopped respawning (dnsmasq, i.e. DNS and DHCP, stayed down) */
+	sigfillset(&allsig);
+	sigprocmask(SIG_BLOCK, &allsig, NULL);
 
 	if (uid) {
 		ERROR("not root, aborting: %m\n");
--- a/service/instance.c	2026-10-17 18:05:45.155335952 -0500
+++ b/service/instance.c	2026-10-17 18:05:45.167335958 -0500
@@ -556,6 +556,16 @@
 		exit(127);
 	}
 
+	/* ujail installs its signal handlers only after loading and parsing, and procd signals
+	 * an instance right after starting it (a reload's SIGHUP): start ujail with signals held,
+	 * it releases them once its handlers are in (jail.c signals_init) */
+	if (in->has_jail) {
+		sigset_t all;
+
+		sigfillset(&all);
+		sigprocmask(SIG_BLOCK, &all, NULL);
+	}
+
 	execvp(argv[0], argv);
 	exit(127);
 }
